{"lines":[{"t":"Reading","x":0.82650069187432296,"y":0.045708513320656508,"h":0.018782276389873176,"c":1,"w":0.082263361612955777},{"t":"football penalty taking. But during a threat state, cortisol inhibits the positive effect","y":0.094395280167117956,"w":0.77207392374674477,"h":0.017523324454428502,"x":0.11704312019803353,"c":1},{"h":0.019306029823325743,"y":0.11179675717733784,"x":0.11904564165847906,"t":"of adrenaline, resulting in tighter blood vessels, higher blood pressure, slower","w":0.73112136840820308,"c":1},{"x":0.11898400110005782,"t":"psychological responses, and a faster heart rate. In short, a threat state makes","y":0.12855545431322901,"w":0.74354090372721349,"h":0.020849150260992766,"c":1},{"h":0.018466040237111625,"x":0.1190298076873042,"y":0.14726590021329899,"t":"people more anxious - they make worse decisions and perform more poorly. In","w":0.74551605224609374,"c":1},{"h":0.021048016393430791,"y":0.16416254418641851,"t":"tennis players, cortisol has been associated with more unsuccessful serves and","x":0.11898391848562691,"w":0.74972935994466139,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.14989733378092443,"y":0.18604651182111143,"t":"greater anxiety.","h":0.014543458494113204,"x":0.11909650757223453},{"y":0.21209439500269867,"t":"That said, anxiety is also a common experience for athletes when they re under","w":0.7494866434733074,"x":0.11909651389905197,"h":0.017699115044247704,"c":1},{"t":"pressure. Anxiety can increase heart rate and perspiration, cause heart palpitations,","c":1,"x":0.11909651525347366,"y":0.22965116281290288,"w":0.79055440266927091,"h":0.017546477078688172},{"w":0.76397928873697929,"y":0.24706328583291037,"h":0.018874049679016291,"c":1,"t":"muscle tremors and shortness of breath, as well as headaches, nausea, stomach","x":0.12109626942155263},{"y":0.26351154827572021,"h":0.020043868793498953,"t":"pain, weakness and a desire to escape in more extreme cases. Anxiety can also","c":1,"x":0.12106271622820448,"w":0.75579330444335935},{"y":0.28197674417429874,"t":"reduce concentration and self-control and cause overthinking. The intensity with","h":0.017441860412777621,"c":1,"w":0.75359344482421864,"x":0.11909650232228927},{"c":1,"w":0.77207392374674477,"h":0.015988371857499573,"y":0.30087209313625918,"x":0.11909650836227835,"t":"which a person experiences anxiety depends on the demands and resources they"},{"h":0.020317403967753278,"t":"have. Anxiety may also manifest itself in the form of excitement or nervousness","y":0.31632467277831988,"c":1,"x":0.11692970333307177,"w":0.7476636759440104},{"h":0.019203451601101595,"c":1,"y":0.33551846320489798,"t":"depending on the stress response. Negative stress responses can be damaging to","w":0.77833429972330725,"x":0.11904901237733952},{"h":0.01978206128145743,"x":0.11904637711746327,"t":"both physical and mental health - and repeated episodes of anxiety coupled with","c":1,"w":0.76396530151367181,"y":0.35250795946734437},{"c":1,"h":0.017699115044247815,"t":"negative responses can increase risk of heart disease and depression.","x":0.12114989940714888,"y":0.37197640100452301,"w":0.66735112508138017},{"t":"But there are many ways athletes can ensure they respond positively under","w":0.71470418294270832,"h":0.018493297880729731,"c":1,"x":0.11699654585749746,"y":0.39926337238844001},{"t":"pressure. Positive stress responses can be promoted through the language that","y":0.4170222037554242,"w":0.75169240315755215,"h":0.019242559562390515,"x":0.12107392352055228,"c":1},{"y":0.43551497774834558,"w":0.76396184285481761,"t":"they and others - such as coaches or parents - use. Psychologists can also help","h":0.018056414331306891,"x":0.11904781563235976,"c":1},{"w":0.78644765218098955,"h":0.017537901886796603,"x":0.12114989053219802,"c":1,"t":"athletes change how they see their physiological responses - such as helping them","y":0.4533923306403016},{"y":0.47079646031660394,"c":1,"h":0.017699115044247815,"t":"see a higher heart rate as excitement, rather than nerves. Developing psychological","w":0.79055440266927091,"x":0.11909651983579569},{"x":0.11909651366210038,"y":0.4898255814182022,"w":0.74127309163411448,"h":0.01754905003010343,"c":1,"t":"skills, such as visualisation, can also help decrease physiological responses to"},{"h":0.016036392594509064,"c":1,"y":0.50726744197167428,"w":0.75564682006835937,"t":"threat. Visualisation may involve the athlete recreating a mental picture of a time","x":0.11909650790940267},{"c":1,"w":0.74552810668945324,"h":0.019929173562378999,"t":"when they performed well, or picturing themselves doing well in the future. This","y":0.5244021137986461,"x":0.11903194559971733},{"c":1,"y":0.54360465127731594,"t":"can help create a feeling of control over the stressful event. Recreating competitive","x":0.12114989022390081,"w":0.77823410034179696,"h":0.015988371857499684},{"h":0.018464985287646618,"t":"pressure during training can also help athletes learn how to deal with stress. An","x":0.12107474155508413,"y":0.56040116483295321,"c":1,"w":0.74756734212239595},{"x":0.12104688888955252,"w":0.76202356974283858,"c":1,"y":0.57712581680463748,"t":"example of this might be scoring athletes against their peers to create a sense of","h":0.020026533863889084},{"x":0.12114990303542887,"y":0.59734513296347791,"t":"competition. This would increase the demands which players experience compared","w":0.7823408508300782,"h":0.016026959939692165,"c":1},{"t":"to a normal training session, while still allowing them to practise coping with stress.","c":1,"w":0.78234085083007809,"x":0.11909651494548569,"y":0.61474926271692121,"h":0.017518179114237586},{"x":0.88090349011993185,"w":0.032854210535685269,"h":0.017441860412777732,"c":1,"t":"45","y":0.92005813949396886},{"h":0.04166666666666663,"w":0.45882354736328113,"y":0.94166666658950615,"c":1,"x":0.51176469618764042,"t":"IELTSXpress.com"}],"h":3390,"w":2400}